{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P979dTbUBoqdUUh7cBoXcp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd069-join\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/join: Join Lines of Two Files on a Common Field\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Shell scripts and data pipelines use join to perform relational join operations on two\n6\t  sorted files based on a common field. The macOS BSD join differs from GNU join in field\n7\t  separator handling, output format options, and header support. The Go implementation must\n8\t  match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gjoin, installed by coreutils) in output and exit\n9\t  codes for all supported flag combinations, verified by differential testing via\n10\t  pkg/testutils. All tests run under LC_ALL=C to avoid locale-dependent collation\n11\t  differences.\n12\t\n13\tgoals:\n14\t  - G1: Join two sorted files on a common join field.\n15\t  - G2: Support configurable field separators, output field selection, and unpairable line handling.\n16\t  - G3: Support header lines and input validation.\n17\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against gjoin via differential testing.\n18\t\n19\trequirements:\n20\t  R1:\n21\t    title: Default join behavior\n22\t    items:\n23\t      - R1.1:\n24\t          text: \"Must read two sorted files and join lines where the join field (default: first field) matches. Must print one output line per matching pair.\"\n25\t      - R1.2:\n26\t          text: \"Fields in each line are separated by whitespace (runs of blanks and tabs) by default. The output separator is a single space by default.\"\n27\t      - R1.3:\n28\t          text: \"Lines that do not pair (present in one file but not the other) are suppressed by default.\"\n29\t      - R1.4:\n30\t          text: \"When one of the file arguments is '-', must read that file from stdin.\"\n31\t\n32\t  R2:\n33\t    title: Field selection and output format\n34\t    items:\n35\t      - R2.1:\n36\t          text: \"-1 FIELD must join on field FIELD of file 1 (fields are numbered from 1). -2 FIELD must join on field FIELD of file 2.\"\n37\t      - R2.2:\n38\t          text: \"-j FIELD must set the join field for both files simultaneously.\"\n39\t      - R2.3:\n40\t          text: \"-o FORMAT must select and order output fields. FORMAT is a comma-separated or space-separated list of FILENUM.FIELDNUM specifiers (e.g., 1.2,2.1) or '0' for the join field.\"\n41\t      - R2.4:\n42\t          text: \"-t CHAR must use CHAR as both the input and output field separator.\"\n43\t\n44\t  R3:\n45\t    title: Unpairable lines and header mode\n46\t    items:\n47\t      - R3.1:\n48\t          text: \"-a FILENUM must also print unpairable lines from file FILENUM (1 or 2). May be specified twice (-a 1 -a 2) to print unpairable lines from both files.\"\n49\t      - R3.2:\n50\t          text: \"-v FILENUM must print only unpairable lines from file FILENUM, suppressing paired lines.\"\n51\t      - R3.3:\n52\t          text: \"-e STRING must replace missing input fields with STRING in the output.\"\n53\t      - R3.4:\n54\t          text: \"--header must treat the first line of each input file as a header line, joining them regardless of sort order and printing the result before data lines.\"\n55\t\n56\t  R4:\n57\t    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n58\t    items:\n59\t      - R4.1:\n60\t          text: Must exit 0 when the join completes successfully.\n61\t      - R4.2:\n62\t          text: Must exit 1 when an invalid option is given or a file cannot be opened.\n63\t      - R4.3:\n64\t          text: \"Differential tests must compare stdout and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils. Tests must use LC_ALL=C for deterministic collation.\"\n65\t      - R4.4:\n66\t          text: \"Tests must cover: default join on first field, -1/-2 field selection, -j combined field, -t custom separator, -o output format, -a unpairable lines, -v unpairable only, -e empty replacement, --header, stdin as one input, and error cases (unsorted input with --check-order, missing file).\"\n67\t\n68\tnon_goals:\n69\t  - cmd/join does not implement locale-aware collation beyond LC_ALL=C behavior.\n70\t  - cmd/join does not implement --nocheck-order to suppress unsorted-input warnings.\n71\t\n72\tacceptance_criteria:\n73\t  - id: AC1\n74\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/join <(printf 'a 1\\\\nb 2\\\\n') <(printf 'a X\\\\nb Y\\\\n') produces 'a 1 X' and 'b 2 Y', matching gjoin.\"\n75\t    traces:\n76\t      - R1.1\n77\t      - R1.2\n78\t      - R4.1\n79\t  - id: AC2\n80\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/join -t ',' -1 2 -2 1 file1 file2 joins on the specified fields with comma separator, matching gjoin.\"\n81\t    traces:\n82\t      - R2.1\n83\t      - R2.4\n84\t  - id: AC3\n85\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/join -a 1 -e EMPTY -o 0,1.2,2.2 file1 file2 prints unpairable lines from file 1 with EMPTY for missing fields, matching gjoin.\"\n86\t    traces:\n87\t      - R2.3\n88\t      - R3.1\n89\t      - R3.3\n90\t  - id: AC4\n91\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/join missing_file file2 exits 1 with error on stderr, matching gjoin.\"\n92\t    traces:\n93\t      - R4.2\n94\t  - id: AC5\n95\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gjoin passes for all flag combinations listed in R4.4.\"\n96\t    traces:\n97\t      - R4.3\n98\t      - R4.4\n99\t  - id: AC6\n100\t    criterion: \"cmd/join compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n101\t    traces:\n102\t      - R1.1\n103\t      - R1.2\n104\t      - R1.3\n105\t      - R1.4\n106\t      - R2.1\n107\t      - R2.2\n108\t      - R2.3\n109\t      - R2.4\n110\t      - R3.1\n111\t      - R3.2\n112\t      - R3.3\n113\t      - R3.4\n114\t      - R4.1\n115\t      - R4.2\n116\t      - R4.3\n117\t      - R4.4\n118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecb35e67-741f-4f50-90cc-dff29e80b28b","uuid":"232cbb8f-fb9a-4bc7-97fc-3ad3bbf2a702","timestamp":"2026-05-22T14:28:35.105Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/d