{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler orchestrator pipeline) has assigned stitch task #5455: create a \"contract\" (stub/skeleton) for `cmd/join` in the go-unix-utils project. The task requires creating two files:\n   - `cmd/join/main.go` — Main entry point with all flag definitions from srd069-join and stub functions that compile but have minimal/empty bodies.\n   - `cmd/join/join_test.go` — Differential test skeleton using `testutils.BuildBinary` and `exec.LookPath(\"gjoin\")` with `t.Skip` fallback and an empty `[]testutils.DiffTest` slice.\n\n   The deliverable is a compilable contract — not a full implementation. Stub functions must have correct signatures but empty or minimal placeholder logic.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils verified via differential testing\n   - Cobbler orchestrator pipeline (measure + stitch phases) for automated code generation\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` pattern for comparing Go binary output against GNU reference binary\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` required at start of every cmd/ main()\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gjoin\")` with `t.Skip` for graceful handling of missing reference binary\n   - LC_ALL=C for deterministic collation in all tests\n   - The `join` utility performs relational joins on two sorted files based on a common field\n   - Git is managed externally — NO git commands allowed\n   - All code must have SPDX copyright header\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max\n   - File size limit: 500 lines max\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd069-join.yaml` (READ)\n     - This is the SRD defining all requirements for the join utility\n     - Flags needed: `-1 FIELD`, `-2 FIELD`, `-j FIELD`, `-o FORMAT`, `-t CHAR`, `-a FILENUM` (can be specified twice), `-v FILENUM`, `-e STRING`, `--header`, `--check-order` (mentioned in R4.4)\n     - Non-goals: no locale-aware collation beyond LC_ALL=C, no `--nocheck-order`\n     - R1: Default join on first field, whitespace separator, suppress unpairable lines, stdin via '-'\n     - R2: Field selection (-1, -2, -j), output format (-o), custom separator (-t)\n     - R3: Unpairable lines (-a, -v), missing field replacement (-e), header mode (--header)\n     - R4: Exit codes (0 success, 1 error), differential testing requirements\n   \n   - `cmd/join/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - Package main with flag parsing for all SRD flags\n     - `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` call at start of main()\n     - Stub functions with correct signatures\n   \n   - `cmd/join/join_test.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - TestDiff skeleton with `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` \n     - `exec.LookPath(\"gjoin\")` with `t.Skip` fallback\n     - Empty `[]testutils.DiffTest` slice\n   \n   - Key existing pkg/ contracts (from project_context, not read via tools):\n     - `pkg/testutils`: `BuildBinary(t, \".\")`, `RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)`, `DiffTest` struct\n     - `pkg/sys`: `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only one tool call was made (Read of the SRD file) before being asked to summarize.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to identify all flags needed for the contract\n   - Was about to write both files when the summary request came in\n   - No problems encountered yet\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive stitch task prompt with full project context, task description for #5455 (cmd/join contract), execution constitution, go style constitution, SRDs, source code, etc.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/join/main.go` with:\n     - Copyright header\n     - Package main\n     - All imports (fmt, os, flag, strings, and github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys)\n     - Flag variable definitions for: -1, -2, -j, -o, -t, -a (can be repeated), -v, -e, --header, --check-order\n     - main() calling sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler(), parsing flags, dispatching to stub functions\n     - Stub functions with correct signatures but minimal bodies\n   - Create `cmd/join/join_test.go` with:\n     - Copyright header\n     - TestDiff skeleton using testutils.BuildBinary and exec.LookPath(\"gjoin\")\n     - Empty test slice\n   - Verify: `go build -o bin/join ./cmd/join/` compiles\n   - Verify: `go vet ./cmd/join/` passes\n   - Verify: `go test ./cmd/join/... -count=1` passes\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd069-join.yaml` to gather the flag specifications needed for the contract. The SRD defines these flags:\n   - `-1 FIELD` (join field for file 1, default 1)\n   - `-2 FIELD` (join field for file 2, default 1)\n   - `-j FIELD` (join field for both files)\n   - `-o FORMAT` (comma/space-separated FILENUM.FIELDNUM or '0')\n   - `-t CHAR` (input and output field separator)\n   - `-a FILENUM` (print unpairable lines from FILENUM, can be specified for both 1 and 2)\n   - `-v FILENUM` (print ONLY unpairable lines from FILENUM)\n   - `-e STRING` (replace missing fields)\n   - `--header` (treat first line as header)\n   - `--check-order` (mentioned in R4.4 test cases)\n   \n   I was about to write both `cmd/join/main.go` and `cmd/join/join_test.go` files.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/join/main.go` and `cmd/join/join_test.go` as specified in the task. The task description states:\n   \n   Files to create:\n   - `cmd/join/main.go` — \"Main entry point with flag definitions and function stubs for all requirement groups\"\n   - `cmd/join/join_test.go` — \"Differential test skeleton with BuildBinary and empty test slice\"\n   \n   Requirements:\n   - R1