e for parsed options and remaining args\n- Short flag parsing handles combined flags (`-ruV`)\n\n**Repeated flag handling (keys example):**\n```go\ntype options struct {\n    // ... other fields\n    keys []keyDef\n}\n\n// In parsing (lines 175-176):\nopts.keys = append(opts.keys, key)\n```\n\n### 5. TestDiff Pattern\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5455/cmd/cut/cut_test.go` (lines 17-94)\n\n```go\nfunc TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n    goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n    refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gcut\")\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n    }\n\n    dir := t.TempDir()\n    writeFile(t, dir, \"fields.txt\", \"a:b:c\\n\")\n\n    // Define normalizers as NormalizeFunc closures\n    binaryNameRe := regexp.MustCompile(`(?:/\\S+/)?g?cut`)\n    normalizeBinaryName := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n        return binaryNameRe.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"cut\"))\n    })\n\n    tests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n        {\n            Name:  \"r4_1_exit_zero_field_stdin\",\n            Args:  []string{\"-d:\", \"-f2\"},\n            Stdin: []byte(\"a:b:c\\n\"),\n        },\n        // ... more test cases\n    }\n\n    testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n```\n\n### 6. Custom Flag Type Pattern for Repeated Flags\nThe codebase uses **slice fields** in the options struct rather than custom flag types:\n\n**Pattern found in cmd/sort/main.go:**\n- Use a slice field: `keys []keyDef` (line 76)\n- Append to it during parsing: `opts.keys = append(opts.keys, key)` (lines 175, 246, 320, 330)\n- Access length/iterate when needed: `if len(opts.keys) > 0` (line 378)\n\n**No custom `IntSlice` or `StringSlice` types** are used anywhere in the cmd/ directories. Instead, the pattern is:\n1. Define a slice field in the options struct\n2. Use `append()` to accumulate values during flag parsing\n3. Validate after parsing completes if needed\n\n**For your `-a FILENUM` repeated flag use case:**\nYou would define:\n```go\ntype options struct {\n    // ... other fields\n    fileNums []int  // or whatever type FILENUM is\n}\n\n// During parsing:\n// When you encounter -a flag:\nfileNum, err := parseFileNum(flagValue)\nif err != nil {\n    return options{}, nil, err\n}\nopts.fileNums = append(opts.fileNums, fileNum)\n```\n\n**All file paths are absolute:**\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5455/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5455/cmd/cut/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5455/cmd/sort/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5455/cmd/cut/cut_test.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5455/go.mod`"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecb35e67-741f-4f50-90cc-dff29e80b28b","uuid":"31252dab-c504-430d-9bd0-d801b35e6410","timestamp":"2026-05-22T14:30:17.347Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5455, I need to understand patterns used in existing cmd/ utilities. Specifically:\n\n1. Find a cmd/ that uses a custom flag type for repeated flags (like IntSlice or similar) — I need to handle `-a FILENUM` which can be specified twice. Look for any custom flag types in cmd/ directories.\n\n2. Read the testutils DiffTest struct definition from pkg/testutils/ to get the exact field names and types.\n\n3. Read one existing cmd/ main.go that has multiple flags (like cmd/sort/main.go or cmd/cut/main.go) to see the copyright header format, import style, and flag parsing pattern.\n\n4. Read one existing cmd/ test file (like cmd/sort/join_test.go or cmd/cut/cut_test.go) to see the exact TestDiff pattern used.\n\n5. Check the go.mod file to ge